9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_s_stretch_epic", "label": "S* \u2014 Stretch epic (freehand paths, .catrobat import, SVG plotting)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 30", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m1_engine_core", "label": "M1 \u2014 Engine core milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 34", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Done 2026-07-16, US-101\u2013US-110. Exit criterion: a generated DST loads correctly in an embroidery viewer and matches golden-file expectations for header, records, jumps, colour changes and terminator."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m2_interpreter_mvp", "label": "M2 \u2014 Interpreter MVP milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 43", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Done 2026-07-31, US-201\u2013US-210. Exit criterion: a hardcoded square/star program produces the expected stitch stream in unit tests and the interpreter is incrementally consumable \u2014 step-by-step consumption yields the same stream as batch execution, with an injected clock for time-based bricks."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m3_walking_skeleton_app", "label": "M3 \u2014 Walking skeleton app milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 54", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pick a bundled sample, run it with live stage preview, export DST via share sheet \u2014 proving the full thread through all layers. Exit criteria: end-to-end sample\u2192preview\u2192DST, a synthetic 50k-stitch design at 60 fps on A15-class hardware, and unit-tested zoom/pan transform math (met without a simulator because StagePreview is a Foundation-only target). The run enum's `failed` case was removed as having no producer, since ADR-018 guarantees the interpreter never halts; failure belongs to the export lifecycle."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m4_block_editor", "label": "M4 \u2014 Block editor milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 69", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tap-to-add palette matching Catroid's flow rather than free-form drag; parameter editing is type-specific and a full Catroid-style formula keyboard is deferred so no editor surface is built for functions the M2 interpreter lacks. Ends with an informal usability session with 3-5 target-age users via TestFlight."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m5_project_management", "label": "M5 \u2014 Project management milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_m6_brick_parity_and_polish", "label": "M6 \u2014 Brick parity & polish milestone", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Polish is an audit, not a build-out, because the M3+ definition of done keeps states, accessibility and strings continuous. Parity target is listed as a checklist early so M6 is not discovering scope."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_engineering_standards", "label": "Engineering standards (Swift Testing, strict concurrency, Bundle.module fixtures)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 9", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Swift Testing not XCTest; tests run in parallel so no shared mutable state or fixed file paths; Swift 6 strict concurrency from day one with Sendable value types and a synchronous isolation-agnostic engine core, leaving actor/@MainActor decisions to the app layer."}, {"id": "docs_roadmap_ui_definition_of_done", "label": "Definition of done for UI stories (M3+)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No hardcoded user-facing strings (String Catalog, leading/trailing layout for ~75 languages incl. RTL); loading/empty/error states ship with the feature; animations respect Reduce Motion; a VoiceOver pass with the stage canvas summarising stitch count, colours and size in mm; 44 pt touch targets; Dynamic Type to AX1 without truncation."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_decisions_adr_027", "target": "docs_decisions_adr_018", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 59", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_m1_engine_core", "target": "docs_roadmap_e1_infrastructure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 34", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_m1_engine_core", "target": "docs_roadmap_e2_embroidery_engine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 34", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_m2_interpreter_mvp", "target": "docs_roadmap_e3_program_model_and_interpreter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line 43", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_roadmap_m3_walking_skeleton_app", "target": "docs_roadmap_e4_stage_and_preview", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ROADMAP.md", "source_location": "line